# Cursor Rules - AI Business Management Platform

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: Next.js 14 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Lucide Icons
- Backend: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy / SQLModel, Pydantic v2
- Database: PostgreSQL (with RLS), Qdrant (Vector DB), Redis (Cache & Queue)
- AI/ML: Prophet, Scikit-learn, PyTorch, LangChain / LlamaIndex, LiteLLM

## Core Development Guidelines
1. Multi-Tenancy: ALWAYS include `tenant_id` on every query and API endpoint.
2. Human-in-the-Loop: Any action involving money, price changes, or bulk updates must go through `approval_queue`.
3. Strict Typing: Enforce full type annotations on all Python and TypeScript functions.
4. Error Handling: Always return standardized API responses: `{ "success": bool, "data": ..., "error": ... }`.
5. Testing: Maintain test coverage for all financial calculation routines and AI routing logic.
